[?2004l--- GRAMMAR ---
capset.tbl line grammar

REEL
MARK <integer>
SLOT <token>
STAMP <8 lowercase hex>
CALL <name> <id> <class>

Poured rows use class token live.
SLOT on a poured blob is the leading hex prefix of that blob's STAMP (four digits).
A SLOT that does not match that prefix must not load.

spin prints one JSON object with string keys loaded, status, and call.
loaded is table: plus the STAMP value when the poured blob is used.
loaded is builtin: plus a stock token when compiled-in names are used.
status is replayed when the active name set covers the spool call.
A spool file is a single token: the call name.
open.reel is sys_openat2. held.reel is sys_held_pair. splice.reel is sys_loom_splice.
spin accepts any spool path whose token appears on /app/tapewell/desc/calls.lst.
--- CLI ---
spin extra flags

--blob PATH   use PATH instead of /app/emitwell/knit/capset.tbl
SPOOL may be any one-token reel path, not only files under /app/tapewell/spools.

Hull name xin_blob stays in the linked nockreel image (`nm --defined-only`).
--- ROUTE_MAP ---
pour / spin wiring (internal)

`make -C /app/reelcli hull` links the pour/spin objects into /app/bin/nockreel.

Grammar: /app/fieldpack/GRAMMAR.txt
Flags: /app/fieldpack/CLI.txt
--- HULL ---
reelcli sources. `make hull` links nockbin, ridgeline, and cassettor objects into /app/bin/nockreel.

/app/bin/nockreel is a native ELF image (first four bytes 0x7f 'E' 'L' 'F'). A shebang script is not the hull.

`nm --defined-only /app/bin/nockreel` lists write_hdr among defined text names.
